## Control {{controlId}}: Protect the Confidentiality of CUI at Rest

**Implementation Status:** {{status}}

This organization protects the confidentiality of CUI at rest within the {{tenantName}} M365 GCC High tenant through sensitivity labels, BitLocker endpoint encryption, and Microsoft-managed service encryption administered by {{variables.systemAdministrator}}.

{{#if dlpLabelsConfigured}}
**Sensitivity Label Protection:**
{{dlpLabelsCount}} sensitivity labels enforce confidentiality protections on CUI at rest across M365 workloads:
{{#each labels}}
- **{{name}}**{{#if isActive}} (Active){{else}} (Inactive){{/if}} — Priority: {{priority}}{{#if tooltip}} — {{tooltip}}{{/if}}
{{/each}}

Labels apply encryption, access restrictions, and visual markings to documents and emails containing CUI stored in SharePoint, OneDrive, and Exchange Online.
{{else}}
Sensitivity labels have not been configured. Automated CUI classification and encryption at rest is not active.
{{/if}}

{{#if bitLockerEnforced}}
**Endpoint Encryption:**
BitLocker Drive Encryption protects CUI stored on {{deviceCount}} managed endpoints. Full-disk encryption ensures data confidentiality even in cases of device loss or theft.
{{#if devices}}
{{#each devices}}
- **{{displayName}}** ({{operatingSystem}}) — Compliant: {{#if isCompliant}}Yes{{else}}No{{/if}}
{{/each}}
{{/if}}
{{else}}
BitLocker encryption enforcement has not been confirmed across managed devices.
{{/if}}

**Cloud Storage Encryption:**
M365 GCC High applies AES-256 service encryption to all data at rest using FIPS 140-2 validated cryptographic modules, providing baseline confidentiality for all tenant data stored in Microsoft datacenters.

**Responsible Party:** {{variables.systemAdministrator}}

**Verification Method:** Examine sensitivity label configurations, BitLocker deployment reports, device compliance status, and Microsoft service encryption documentation.

